            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Assassination</strong><br>\nKennedy was assassinated in Dallas, Texas, on November 22, 1963, leaving the nation and the world in shock. His death has been the subject of numerous conspiracy theories.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Kennedy's Policies</strong><br>\nKennedy's policies and initiatives, such as the Peace Corps and efforts to limit nuclear weapons, had lasting impacts on American society and foreign policy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nKennedy's legacy includes his inspirational rhetoric, the idealistic vision of \"Camelot,\" and a renewed sense of American patriotism and public service. His life and presidency have been intensely scrutinized and idealized in popular culture.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
